This PR improves pre-push OPF redaction performance by batching OpenAI Privacy Filter (OPF) inference across **all redactable blobs in all unpushed `entire/checkpoints/v1` commits**, reducing repeated model loads and keeping the privacy “fail-closed” contract intact.

**Changes:**
- Added a new batched redaction API (`BatchBytesWithPrivacyFilter`) plus a helper to estimate batch size (`SumProseLeafBytes`).
- Refactored the v1 pre-push rewrite to collect redactable blobs once, run a single OPF batch, then rebuild commits using cached redacted bytes; added new batch-size and raw-memory caps.
- Updated security/privacy documentation to describe the new batching behavior and the new batch-size cap.

